# ── Bootstrap-only: how to reach Infisical ────────────────────────────────────
# Owner directive 2026-09-18: Infisical is the sole source of truth for every secret. No
# `.env` files anywhere — this `.env.example` is bootstrap-only (machine-identity credentials
# + the encryption master key). Operator knobs, feature flags, provider keys, broker creds, RAG
# fuses, and per-lane budgets all moved out: they live in Infisical (shared / shared-at-ct /
# app projects), per-user Settings (Accounts / 1 / LLM models / Data sources / Notifications),
# or in-code defaults with sane fallbacks. See docs/secrets.md + docs/rollouts/
# 2026-09-18-strict-infisical-no-env-files.md for the full rationale and the loader test
# (test/no-env-loader-or-dotenv-yaml.test.ts) that grep-blocks any regression.
#
# Local development: run `npm run dev:secrets` (Infisical runner). The plain `npm run dev`
# script still exists for unit/E2E tests where no credentials are needed; `predev` warns when
# neither SECRETS_SOURCE nor a bootstrap identity (env or Keychain) is in scope.
#
# Bootstrap resolution precedence at the runner: explicit process env > .env.local > the
# owner's macOS login Keychain (generic passwords, service `socratic-trade-bootstrap`, account =
# the env var name; Infisical client credentials + ALIASES only). Add one with:
#   security add-generic-password -U -s socratic-trade-bootstrap -a INFISICAL_ST_CLIENT_ID -w
# The retired flat key file is never read (owner, 2026-10-18, OPS-818). The
# runner masks Bootstrap values to the end of the app, so a stale `.env.local` cannot restore
# a long-lived credential inside the running app. Cloud VMs and CI use process env instead.

# Infisical machine identity — universal auth (long-lived Client ID + Client Secret). The runner
# exchanges the pair for a short-lived access token automatically. IMPORTANT: the Client Secret
# is NOT the access token — do NOT paste a 64-char Client Secret into INFISICAL_TOKEN (that
# yields "malformed token" 403). App secrets live in the `Socratic-Trade` project (slug
# `socratic-trade`); shared App-A/B (congress-trade) secrets live in `shared-at-ct`.
INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID=39d93bb7-76f9-498c-8b50-a7def52e072f
INFISICAL_CLIENT_ID=
INFISICAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# …or supply a pre-minted access token instead of the Client ID/Secret pair. NOT recommended —
# it expires (see the identity's Access Token TTL); prefer the pair above so the runner re-mints.
INFISICAL_TOKEN=
INFISICAL_ENV=prod
INFISICAL_PATH=/
# Optional for EU Cloud or self-hosted Infisical. The runner passes it only to CLI helpers and
# masks it from the app (default CLI domain is the US Cloud endpoint).
INFISICAL_DOMAIN=
INFISICAL_WATCH=false
# Watch mode gives the third-party CLI only a minimal runtime environment. Put all credentials
# needed by a watched app in Infisical; unrelated shell/provider credentials are deliberately
# not inherited.
# Optional shared project (App-A/B / congress-trade secrets). Setting INFISICAL_SHARED_PROJECT_ID
# makes the runner pull BOTH projects and merge them with the APP project winning any overlapping
# key; give the shared project its OWN machine identity (its own Client ID + Secret).
INFISICAL_SHARED_PROJECT_ID=
INFISICAL_SHARED_CLIENT_ID=
INFISICAL_SHARED_CLIENT_SECRET=
INFISICAL_SHARED_TOKEN=

# ── Encryption master key (still required) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Master key for AES-256-GCM encryption of per-user API keys stored in the DB
# (user_api_keys table). MUST be a stable 32-byte hex string (64 hex chars), and MUST be set for
# any persistent/multi-user deployment: if unset, a RANDOM key is generated per process, so
# every previously-stored key becomes undecryptable after a restart. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Boot guard arming (prod / staged envs only) ──────────────────────────────────
# When set, the app refuses to boot unless launched through the secrets-manager runner (see
# src/lib/secrets-source.ts + scripts/coolify-prod-start.sh phase-2 export). Local dev, tests,
# and CI: leave UNSET. Prod Coolify `socratic-app`: SET (the boot script also sets it, as a
# belt-and-suspenders second arm). Escape hatch: unset and rebuild.
REQUIRE_SECRETS_MANAGER=

# ── Operator knobs that moved OUT of `.env.example` (where to find them now) ─────
# Every operator knob, feature flag, provider key, broker credential, RAG fuse, and per-lane
# budget that used to live in this file moved to one of three homes on 2026-09-18:
#
#   1. Infisical (shared / shared-at-ct / app projects).  Shared fleet coordination keys
#      (`AGENT_SYNC_*`, Slack bot token, the shared Coolify read-only stats token) belong ONLY
#      in the shared project; LLM runtime keys are NOT in Infisical (they belong on the
#      user's Connections page per AGENTS.md "No LLM runtime keys in Infisical for this app").
#
#   2. Per-account user Settings: Settings -> LLM models, Settings -> Data sources, Settings
#      -> Notifications, Settings -> Account & Settings (iOS). Per-user policy + budgets.
#
#   3. In-code defaults with sane fallbacks (e.g. `VECTOR_EMBED_BATCH_DELAY_MS=21000`,
#      `SEC_FILING_INGEST_TTL_HOURS=24`). When the env is unset, the default applies.
#
# If a knob you remember seeing here is not listed in any of those three homes, it is
# intentionally gone — ping me before re-adding it (the CI guard test/no-env-loader-or-
# dotenv-yaml.test.ts blocks regressions).